Batched inference for SpliceAI is an independent, substantially modified
implementation. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by Illumina. The
SpliceAI name is used only to identify compatibility with the upstream
software.

Upstream provenance
-------------------

The inference preparation and score post-processing logic is adapted from
SpliceAI 1.3.1, released on 2020-03-07:

- repository tag: v1.3.1
- tag commit: b3c7f17b4137cb32b30c56c064f8b90b9b8f38d0
- source distribution:
  https://pypi.org/project/spliceai/1.3.1/
- source distribution SHA-256:
  65c76b012ffd2ca97ca96d7f4c0897c78b9aba4d4ca4068331f7fb5cd5c3b7e1
- upstream copyright: Copyright (c) 2013-2018 Illumina, Inc.
- upstream source license: GNU GPL version 3 or later

This work was modified in 2026 to add cross-variant batching,
reference-prediction reuse, length-grouped indel inference, bounded streaming,
deterministic execution, corrected minus-strand output orientation, MANE
conversion, validation utilities, reference-derived variant generation, and
restartable HPC orchestration.

